Methods first published in this repository, with the release that introduced
them (see CHANGELOG.md and docs/architecture.md):

  - Stigmergic coordination of LLM agent swarms through a semantic field whose
    channels evolve by advection-diffusion-reaction on the problem graph, with
    a CFL-style stability bound that clamps the update step (0.1.0)
  - A shadow twin that admits a change to swarm coordination policy only after
    it beats the live policy on replayed scenarios under common random
    numbers (0.1.0)
  - Intent compilation of human goals into a soft reward plus hard rules that
    block plans outright, kept outside the learning loop (0.1.0)
  - Gate-aware plan selection: among near-best plans, prefer the one a gate
    predicts a human will approve (0.1.0)
  - One QUBO interface across exact, simulated-annealing and quantum solvers
    for coordination and scheduling subproblems (0.1.0)

